Revision history for RPi-I2C

3.1803 UNREL
    - Added t/10-validation.t: HW-free unit coverage of new() address
      validation, the _set_reg() register default, and the current
      read_bytes()/write_word() behaviour (pinned via a faked object + stubbed
      XS reads/writes - no bus, no device)
    - Fix _readBlockData() XSUB: croak() on SMBus read failure instead of
      falling through to sv_setpvn() with length -1 (a (STRLEN)-1 over-read
      that could segfault the interpreter)
    - new() now croaks "could not open <dev>" with errno when the device file
      can't be opened (was: "Can't bless non-reference value"), and the ioctl
      croak states the real failure (ioctl(I2C_SLAVE_FORCE) + errno) instead
      of claiming device absence - with I2C_SLAVE_FORCE that ioctl succeeds
      even on an empty bus; absence detection is check_device()'s job. New
      HW-free tests in t/10-validation.t cover both paths
    - POD: fix the config.txt directive for enabling the I2C bus
      (ram=i2c_arm=on -> dtparam=i2c_arm=on); fix "examples direcory" typo;
      document the 32-byte SMBus block cap (silent clamp) on both
      read_block() and write_block()
    - Add t/10-validation.t to MANIFEST - it was never added when the test
      file landed, so the dist tarball would have shipped without it
      (found via post-build RELEASE_TESTING manifest.t; the build artifacts
      themselves were already covered by MANIFEST.SKIP)
    - Add GitHub Actions CI workflow (ubuntu-only matrix - the dist builds
      against the kernel's i2c interface, no wiringPi required; XS build
      step before prove -b; modeled on rpi-pwm-pca9685's workflow)
    - Add examples/arduino.ino to MANIFEST - the POD's UNIT TESTS section
      points users at the sketch but tarballs omitted it; manifest.t never
      noticed because the unanchored .o$ skip pattern matched "arduino.ino".
      Tighten the artifact skip patterns to \.bs$/\.c$/\.o$ and add \.so$
      (previously covered only by the sloppy .o$ match), and skip
      ^\.github/ (CI config stays out of the tarball, matching the other
      rpi-* dists)
    - License unified to Artistic 2.0 - Makefile.PL said GPL_2 while the
      POD said "same terms as Perl itself"; both now artistic_2, matching
      the newer RPi:: dists
    - BREAKING: read_bytes() now returns the documented array of N bytes,
      ascending from the base register (was: a single integer - only the
      base-register byte - due to a (0 << 8) overwrite bug)
    - BREAKING: write_word() and process() now take ($value, [$reg]) like
      write_byte(), with the register optional and defaulting to 0x00 via
      _set_reg() (was: ($reg, $value) with no default, contradicting the
      POD)
    - write_block() now croaks when given more than 32 bytes instead of
      silently truncating (SMBus block-transfer limit)
    - Version bumped 3.1802 -> 3.1803 to mark the API contract break
      (3.1802 was never released; all of its entries ship here)
    - Regenerate bundled ppport.h with Devel::PPPort 3.68 (was 3.20,
      generated 2013 under perl 5.18.2 - predating every perl in the new
      CI matrix); its self-audit reports I2C.xs needs no compat shims at
      all, making the include a removal candidate (backlogged)
    - new() now validates the address range: anything above 0x7F croaks
      (I2C addresses are 7-bit); address 0x00 (general call) remains legal
      by design - RPi::PWM::PCA9685->reset() depends on it for SWRST

3.1801    2026-06-12
    - Exit Makefile.PL gracefully on non-Linux platforms (NA instead of
      FAIL) since the module requires the Linux I2C interface

2.3608  2019-06-27
    - No functional changes
    - Add return values to all methods (closes #9)

2.3607 2018-10-02
    - update croak() error in XS read_block() to ask user if I2C speed too
      high if a fatal error occurs (closes #8)
    - remove erroneous print statement from read_block() (closes #7)
    - fix croak() call in new() where we weren't correctly translating the
      decimal addr to hex before displaying the error message (fixes #6)

2.3606  2018-05-29
    - re-wrote readI2cBlockData() in order to gracefully handle a panic
      situation when the I2C device is no longer available (fixes #4)
    - established new I2C_TESTING env var for RPi::WiringPi's I2C
      exception testing (bypasses croak() if I2C device not found)
    - refactored the logic in new() for establishing I2C connection. It now
      properly croak()s if device not found on the bus

2.3605  2018-02-09
    - fix typo in POD (closes #3)
    - made more clear the warning if having issues communicating with an
      Arduino (closes #5)

2.3604  2017-06-28
    - removed WiringPi::API from being a prereq
    - POD fixes
    - added UNIT TESTS section in POD to explain why there's no unit tests
      for this distribution
    - remove useless int param in XS readByte(), throwing a compiler warning

2.3603  2017-06-23
    - completely changed the way we work. We do not use wiringPi for this
      anymore due to lack of options
    - major POD overhaul
    - added several examples using I2C to an Arduino (Trinket Pro or Uno).
      This provides examples for nearly every function. Internally in the
      Arduino sketch, on the write functions, we save the data to EEPROM,
      where the data can be fetched back out at a certain register to make
      comparisons on (this functionality will be incorporated into the
      RPi::WiringPi unit test suite)

2.3601  2017-06-22
    - First version, released on an unsuspecting world.

